UnitVoter::AllocateGauges
├── when the caller is not approved or owner of the tokenId
│   └── it should revert with NotAuthorized
├── when the chain is not registered
│   └── it should revert with ChainNotActiveOrSunset
├── when the chain is chain zero
│   └── it should revert with ChainNotActiveOrSunset
├── when the chain is paused or suspended
│   └── it should revert with ChainNotActiveOrSunset
├── when the chain is sunset and the gauge list carries only the deallocation sentinel
│   ├── it should flag the dispatch to charge the deallocation return
│   └── it should dispatch one AllocateGauge message to the chain
├── when the chain is sunset and the gauge list carries a non deallocation entry
│   └── it should revert with SunsetDeallocOnly
├── when the chain is sunset and the gauge list is empty
│   └── it should revert with SunsetDeallocOnly
├── when the destination gas limit is zero for a non root chain
│   └── it should revert with MissingDestinationGasLimit
├── when the token has been withdrawn
│   └── it should revert with StakeWithdrawn
├── when the gauge list is invalid
│   ├── when gauges are not strictly ascending
│   │   └── it should revert with GaugesNotStrictlyAscending
│   └── when a gauge allocation amount is zero
│       └── it should revert with ZeroAllocation
├── when the gauge list is valid
│   ├── it should snapshot the live stake into the dispatched message
│   ├── it should stamp the global emissions per VP scalar onto the message
│   ├── it should dispatch one AllocateGauge message to the chain
│   └── it should emit the GaugesAllocated event carrying the gauge array
├── when the gauge total exceeds the booked chain allocation
│   └── it should revert with ChainAllocationMismatch
├── when the gauge total is below the booked chain allocation
│   └── it should revert with ChainAllocationMismatch
├── when the gauge total equals the booked chain allocation
│   ├── it should snapshot the live stake into the dispatched message
│   ├── it should stamp a zero emissions per VP scalar when the total weight is zero
│   └── it should dispatch one AllocateGauge message to the chain
├── when the gauge list is empty
│   └── it should dispatch one AllocateGauge message to the chain when the booked allocation is zero
├── when the deallocation sentinel amount pushes the total over the booked chain allocation
│   └── it should revert with ChainAllocationMismatch
├── when the deallocation sentinel amount brings the total to the booked chain allocation
│   ├── it should forward the full value to the orchestrator
│   └── it should dispatch one AllocateGauge message to the chain
├── when the gauge list carries only the deallocation sentinel
│   ├── it should forward the full value to the orchestrator
│   └── it should flag the dispatch to charge the deallocation return
├── when the stake is expired and the gauge list carries only the deallocation sentinel
│   └── it should dispatch one AllocateGauge message to the chain
├── when the stake is expired and the gauge list carries a non deallocation entry
│   └── it should revert with StakeExpired
├── when the stake is expired and the gauge list is empty
│   └── it should revert with StakeExpired
├── when no deallocation sentinel is present
│   ├── it should forward the full value to the orchestrator
│   └── it should leave the dispatch unflagged
├── when the dispatch synchronously returns the deallocation
│   ├── it should process the deallocation return within the same call
│   └── it should credit the returned amount to chain zero
├── when the live stake shape differs from the stored root shape
│   └── it should revert with StaleShape
├── when a stale shape is reconciled with an empty chain allocation
│   ├── it should re-anchor the stored root shape to the live stake
│   └── it should let the retried gauge allocation dispatch
└── when a prior total weight change left the global emissionsPerVP stale
    ├── it should ship the freshly resampled emissionsPerVP in the dispatched message
    └── it should resample the stored global emissionsPerVP against the current total weight
